{
  "requirement": "An execution error returns `Err` rather than a `Fingerprinted` containing a\ncompleted answer.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has one obligation: when execution fails, `verify` returns `Err`, not a `Fingerprinted` holding a completed answer. The reviewed tests check it at several failure points.\n\n- **Procedure failure:** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[loading_execution_resolution_and_saving_failures_do_not_publish_answers]` sets `review.failure = Some(\"execute\")` and asserts `verify` returns `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"execute\"))`.\n- **Failures inside execution:** the same test covers a read of a missing node (`Graph(\"missing\")`) and an edge-resolution failure (`Graph(\"edges\")`). Both make `verify` return `Err`.\n- **Missing agent:** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` asserts `verify` returns `Err(ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured)` and that no record is stored.\n- **Callback failure:** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]` has a read inside the callback fail. It asserts `Err(Graph(\"missing\"))` and that no records are stored.\n- **Contrast cases:** the tests also show that `verify` still returns `Ok` when no execution error occurs. In `loading_execution_resolution_and_saving_failures_do_not_publish_answers`, a failed load does not stop a later successful `verify`. In `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence`, decode errors from loading do not stop a new execution from returning a value.\n- **Non-execution errors:** storage and serialization failures, such as `serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged` and the storage-test `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors`, are not execution errors. They mostly check neighbouring requirements, so the subject does not depend on them.\n\nThe assertions use `matches!` on the specific `Err` variants, so an implementation that returned `Ok` with a completed answer would fail them. I found no uncovered execution-error scenario that the text names.",
